    "alert_id": "EX3_002",
    "title": "DTG hyperglycemia risk factors present",
    "message": "Guidelines list risk factors for DTG-associated hyperglycemia: age ≥30, BMI ≥25 kg/m², family history of DM, and hypertension. This patient is 45 and has BMI 33, meeting two risk factors. Guidelines state clients with ≥2 risk factors and normal baseline glucose should have RBS or FBS monitored every 3 months for 6 months. Current fasting glucose 5.6 mmol/L is normal, but no evidence of prior serial glucose monitoring exists. The dyslipidemia pattern (LDL 4.2, total cholesterol 6.4, triglycerides 2.3) further supports metabolic risk that compounds DTG hyperglycemia concern.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
