    "alert_id": "EX3_003",
    "title": "TDF renal monitoring overdue by 2 months",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR every 12 months for experienced patients on TDF. The last creatinine was 196 days ago (2025-08-12), so the annual check is not yet overdue. However, no eGFR was recorded alongside the creatinine. The clinician's plan includes no renal monitoring orders today. Given the patient's rising BMI and metabolic abnormalities, ensuring complete renal screening per protocol is advisable. Creatinine 72 umol/L was normal, providing reassurance against current renal dysfunction.",
